      "In Dott. Flavio Bruno’s reading, the dog used by the Roman world for war, guarding, hunting, and rural work should not be imagined as a creature that disappears with the legions. Qualities selected because they were useful — mobility, presa, courage, the ability to accompany people, vigilance, and readiness for action — could be reabsorbed into civilian and rural society.",
